id: pm-rust-s6j4
title: Extend native orientation to richer context sections and relationship packets
description: "Follow-up to the native brief orientation slice: implement context intents, deeper sections, calendar recurrence and timezone handling, workspace-memory rollups, derived-snapshot recovery, dependency relationship-context packets, richer history projections and canonical output continuation controls. Keep unsupported requests explicit until each contract has exact oracle differentials."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[3]: follow-up,orientation,rust
created_at: "2026-10-18T03:44:38.720Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-19T22:31:17.353Z"
assignee: codex-agent
claim_principal: codex-agent
author: codex-agent
parent: pm-rust-u4al
comments[44]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-18T05:11:47.743Z",codex-agent,"Deferred orientation scope also includes richer extension discovery policy, nonminimal manifest controls and execution of declared context_relevance service overrides. The core native slice fails closed on these boundaries instead of executing extension code. Future acceptance must cover configured enable/disable policy, version/engine bounds, contribution inventories and scorer activation against the pinned oracle."
  "2026-10-19T12:26:44.135Z",codex-agent,"Scope: native default and deep context sections, relationship packets, producer continuation and output parity against the locked oracle. Preserve projection-based reads from #94. Validate synthetic fixtures and an immutable real tracker copy; publish aggregate timing only. The broader follow-up description remains beyond this bounded task."
  "2026-10-19T12:42:00.295Z",codex-agent,"Implementation in progress: preserve the brief metadata projection; add selected deep-section fields, descendant completion, retained compact activity, files/workload/staleness/test summaries and ranked continuation. Relationship packets use deps --format context, matching the pinned command contract. The immutable real copy contains 1254 items at capture. Initial parity exposed the existing static extension-health refusal for inert manifest metadata; extending that read boundary. Synthetic dependencies retain created_at because the locked oracle has the already tracked timestamp-sort defect."
  "2026-10-19T13:17:21.187Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: replace only Workspace::context_with_global with its origin/main implementation, leaving the new regression and all other functions intact. cargo +1.90.0 test --locked --lib orientation_context::tests::deep_sections_preserve_relationships_and_evidence -- --exact fails behaviorally (0 passed, 1 failed; exit 101) because deep native context is refused. Restore the implementation byte-for-byte: the identical command passes (1 passed, 0 failed; exit 0). Expanded context oracle matrix and bounded relationship packet matrix each pass independently. Preserve the locked oracle quirks: legacy depends_on is ignored by blocker detail resolution; packet token settlement excludes subsequently attached alias counts; infeasible packet roots remain unknown_error refusals. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-19T13:29:17.045Z",codex-agent,"Validation checkpoint: the native deep-section regression passes, its single-function behavioral revert fails, all 30 real-copy comparisons passed with authoritative hashes unchanged, and both expanded context and relationship-packet oracle matrices passed independently. Added conservative extension minimum-version and supported-field validation so the static summary retains explicit boundaries rather than accepting unsupported controls. Preparing a draft PR to run the unchanged cross-platform release gates while final coverage and release-binary measurements continue. The item remains claimed and in progress."
  "2026-10-19T13:34:37.683Z",codex-agent,"Added an independent 201-item oracle regression for the completion rounding boundary: JavaScript computes Math.round(29 / 200 * 100) as 14. Native completion now preserves the IEEE division-and-rounding sequence before producing its integer field. The linked test wrapper accepts an optional integration suite while retaining sanitized compiler/test output. Final release measurements will use the frozen binary after these boundary fixes."
  "2026-10-19T13:38:09.456Z",codex-agent,"The first full instrumented run reached the orientation suite with its preceding suites passing, then exposed an obsolete deferred-option assertion: context --after and packet --cursor/--direction/--kind are now implemented. Updated only that deferral inventory; positive oracle comparisons cover the supported controls. Independent 201-item completion-rounding oracle regression passes. Current strict Clippy passes. Draft PR #97 now carries the implementation; final gate totals and measurements remain pending."
  "2026-10-19T13:38:25.120Z",codex-agent,"Correction to the preceding checkpoint: the draft is PR #98, https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/pull/98. The #97 reference in that checkpoint was incorrect. The implementation branch remains feat/native-context-sections."
  "2026-10-19T13:59:14.815Z",codex-agent,"Additional numeric regression proof: reverting only completion and packet-budget arithmetic to integer shortcuts produced 41 passing and 2 failing orientation unit tests; restoring the implementation produced 43 passing and 0 failing tests. The pinned oracle uses IEEE floating-point evaluation, including 29/200 completion rendering as 14 percent and a 470/846 budget reduction producing 234. Added blocked-fallback deep differentials and explicit packet refusal comparisons; preserving the published raw TypeError text and JSON unknown_error envelope for infeasible packet budgets. No oracle pin or gate threshold changed."
  "2026-10-19T14:05:19.198Z",codex-agent,"All three linked test commands passed: 1 native deep regression, 5 packet unit tests, and 1 independent completion oracle regression. Test-result tracking is disabled by project policy, so this comment records the aggregate result without changing that policy. Fresh-clone health with isolated Git identity and required merge drivers passes. Expanded the real-copy harness to compare representative relationship roots, encodings, bounds and continuation in addition to the 30 context comparisons. Added custom activity-limit, retained-history failure propagation and stale-order section coverage; no runtime dependency or threshold changes."
  "2026-10-19T14:14:06.555Z",codex-agent,"Focused branch instrumentation now passes 44 orientation unit tests. The retained-activity iterator boundary was extracted so its original real filesystem error and propagation can be exercised without SDK mocks or timing-dependent directory races. Ordinary exact-head CI passed all 501 tests on Linux and macOS; full instrumented aggregate gates remain pending. Recorded the isolated Windows list-latency ceiling miss on existing performance item pm-rust-wdj4; context itself passed that job. The final real-copy measurement will use the rebuilt production binary, with no mixing of binary hashes."
  "2026-10-19T14:18:39.032Z",codex-agent,"The full Linux aggregate at 921275d ran 501 ordinary and 501 instrumented tests successfully, then correctly rejected coverage: seven missed regions and one missed branch. Added targeted cases for the reported activity limit, stale sorting, history propagation, unknown extension-control branch and invalid packet direction through Workspace::deps. The updated 44-test orientation unit run passes; the unchanged complete coverage gate will be rerun on the next head. All three platforms passed the ordinary 501-test suite. No exclusion, threshold, dependency pin or latency ceiling was changed."
  "2026-10-19T14:40:54.395Z",codex-agent,"Count correction and current-source checkpoint: ordinary CI at 365d805 passed 502 tests on Linux, 498 on macOS and 493 on Windows, each across 20 suites with zero failures or ignored tests. Platform-specific test selections explain the differences; earlier comments using the Linux count for every platform were imprecise. All three unchanged latency jobs passed, including context p95 of 118.27 ms, 126.46 ms and 213.52 ms respectively below the 250 ms ceiling. Full aggregate coverage jobs remain pending. Bun orientation passed all 24 tests on the earlier binary; the same suite is rerunning against the final production source. The real-copy harness timestamp flag is now scoped to context rather than packet reads."
  "2026-10-19T14:51:43.654Z",codex-agent,"The complete instrumented Linux and macOS runs at 365d805 passed their test suites and reached 100 percent functions and branches, but rejected one remaining activity-iterator line/region. Changed the private iterator boundary from generic specialization to one borrowed iterator implementation, so the real filesystem-error test and production reads exercise the same function. Strengthened nested descendant and progress-order fixtures plus original I/O kind/path assertions. The updated stable orientation unit run passes all 44 tests. Rebuilt the optimized binary and restarted final-source Bun acceptance and real-copy comparisons; interrupted runs are not counted as passing final evidence. Coverage thresholds and source scope remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T15:00:07.127Z",codex-agent,"At 63d359e, the 44-test focused instrumented orientation run passes. Both new modules, orientation_context/sections.rs and orientation_deps/packet.rs, now measure 100 percent lines, functions, regions and branches without exclusions or threshold changes. Strict Clippy passes. The frozen optimized binary passed all 26 real-copy relationship comparisons across two representative roots, including TOON/JSON, summary, incoming traversal, node/token limits and three cursor pages per root. The combined real-copy run is now executing its context matrix and will verify authoritative hashes at completion. Whole-crate aggregate gates remain pending on this head."
  "2026-10-19T15:06:13.552Z",codex-agent,"Final-source acceptance and real-copy measurement passed at implementation head 63d359e. Bun ran all 24 orientation differential tests with zero failures or ignored tests. All three linked commands passed again: seven underlying test executions, with evidence recording unchanged at project tracking_disabled policy. The optimized binary passed 56 complete stdout/stderr/status comparisons: 30 context and 26 packet cases across two roots. The captured real tracker had 1254 items rather than the earlier stated 1251; all 2527 authoritative item/history files retained their hashes. Thirty alternating fresh-process samples per runtime/command: default native p50/p95 81.0/291.0 ms versus pinned TS 1402.2/5101.8 ms; deep native 445.7/598.0 ms versus TS 1905.0/2684.5 ms. The clock-pinned driver disables the scheduling-dependent packing guard; the shared-host results are bounded measurements, not a scale guarantee. Aggregate receipt: docs/benchmarks/native-context-sections-2026-10-19.json. Whole-crate CI gates remain pending."
  "2026-10-19T15:24:51.243Z",codex-agent,"Complete unchanged release gates PASSED at 63d359e on all three platforms: Linux 502 ordinary plus 502 instrumented tests, macOS 498 plus 498, Windows 493 plus 493, each across 40 suite executions with zero failures or ignored tests. Every platform measures 100 percent lines/functions/regions/branches. Linux exact totals: 13074 lines, 1349 functions, 21821 regions, 3148 branches, all covered. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, required pinned-oracle suites, audit under the existing advisory policy, changelog verification and clone-local merge-driver/strict tracker health checks passed. All nine CI jobs and CodeQL are green. Gate receipt: docs/benchmarks/native-context-gates-2026-10-19.json; run: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39273842181. The measured Rust source is frozen; only aggregate receipts, documentation and tracker handoff remain to commit."
  "2026-10-19T15:24:55.910Z",codex-agent,"Handoff: the requested native sections and relationship-packet slice is implemented in PR #98, Serve pm context natively with relationship packets. Exact fixture and real-copy parity, both behavioral revert proofs, final-source Bun acceptance, full unchanged cross-platform gates and the real-copy timing table are documented. Existing advanced intent/filter/scorer/recurrence, large workspace-memory and stale-snapshot boundaries remain explicit; pinned TS inconsistencies are documented and no upstream issue was filed. Releasing ownership with pause leaves this item open for the orchestrator to verify and close. Do not merge or publish. The final evidence-only commit will receive CI verification of the unchanged Rust source and updated metadata."
  "2026-10-19T16:15:15.371Z",codex-agent,"PR 98 review round 1: verify all three CodeRabbit findings against the pinned oracle, add behavioral revert proofs, fix Windows context latency without changing bounds, and certify the three-OS release matrix. Ubuntu job 118147020360 was cancelled after its test step passed; Windows job 118147020130 measured context p95 339.5ms against 250ms."
  "2026-10-19T16:20:25.153Z",codex-agent,"All three review findings are valid. External graph namespace allocation now matches the pinned oracle, including collisions with local and dangling IDs. The new differential passed eight full/summary TOON/JSON cases with plain global/external targets and URL controls. Four harness regressions passed; isolated behavioral reversions for argument validation, root namespace filtering, and latency warm-up each failed. Run history: context p95 186.188ms at 63d359e versus 339.541ms at 506b448 with identical Rust source and latency harness; 365d805 measured 213.515ms. Adopt five warm-ups and a fixed median of three 30-launch p95 windows, retaining all samples and the 50/150/250ms bounds. No retry-until-green. Preserve pinned quirks tracked upstream by pm-cli issues 1509 through 1513."
  "2026-10-19T16:22:35.146Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs completed: reverting only Graph::new to head 506b448 makes packet_external_namespace_keys fail (exit 101); restoring passes 1/1. Reverting only required-option token rejection or source_kind-aware root filtering fails the respective Node regression (exit 1). Removing warm-up or replacing median-window aggregation with a single window also fails (exit 1); restored Node harness passes 4/4. No threshold, coverage scope or oracle pin changed. The graph differential passed 8 full/summary TOON/JSON comparisons. The latest review body contains no outside-diff findings."
  "2026-10-19T16:24:27.951Z",codex-agent,"Ubuntu root cause confirmed from check-run annotations: job 118147020360 exceeded its 15-minute maximum, although cargo test passed before cleanup. Give every ordinary Rust matrix job the existing 20-minute Windows allowance for setup, test and cleanup. The separate 35-minute full release aggregate and all latency/coverage bounds remain unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T16:25:26.511Z",codex-agent,"Local validation: strict all-target Clippy passed; all five linked commands passed (13 underlying test executions, including four Node harness tests); project test-result tracking remains disabled by its existing policy. Changelog regeneration and check passed. Normal-environment strict health sees an existing extension host-version skew between the pinned CLI and an installed pm-github extension; do not change pins or extension policy. Verify strict health in a clean clone with isolated home and clone-local merge drivers, matching CI."
  "2026-10-19T16:32:25.440Z",codex-agent,"Fresh no-local clone at ceffe36 passed health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit with isolated home/Git configuration and no tracked changes. This is the CI health scope, not a full history-drift audit. The first Bun acceptance attempt overlapped oracle extraction and failed on a missing dependency; it is excluded from passing evidence. Oracle installation completed and the entire 25-test Bun orientation suite is rerunning. Full local isolated-identity just release-check and CI run 39285340550 are pending."
  "2026-10-19T16:37:59.753Z",codex-agent,"GitHub reports an active Actions/Pages/Webhooks incident with workflow processing and status-update delays: https://www.githubstatus.com/incidents/8tzbpcnl75jp . CI run 39285340550 metadata is delayed; completed steps are not treated as a final passing job conclusion. Continue local validation and await definitive three-OS aggregate receipts."
  "2026-10-19T16:39:27.252Z",codex-agent,"End-to-end context-real harness smoke passed on a fully initialized synthetic tracker and a frozen debug binary: 37 exact comparisons (11 packet, 26 context) across one local relationship root. Authoritative hashes and the binary hash remained unchanged. One timing sample per runtime was only a smoke check, not performance certification. The macOS CI latency step passed all unchanged bounds: get 14.254ms, list 80.009ms, context 135.623ms. Final GitHub job conclusions and full aggregate gates remain pending during the status-update incident."
  "2026-10-19T16:41:15.865Z",codex-agent,"All three CI latency step logs passed the unchanged 50/150/250ms get/list/context ceilings with fixed three-window measurement. Context median-window p95: Linux 105.985ms, macOS 135.623ms, Windows 188.520ms. All raw window samples remain in CI logs. Full release aggregates and definitive GitHub check conclusions remain pending."
  "2026-10-19T16:50:26.305Z",codex-agent,"Completed Bun acceptance: PM_NODE_INTERPRETER=bun PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential passed 25/25 with zero failures or ignored tests (Bun 1.3.5). All ordinary CI jobs passed: Linux 505, macOS 501, Windows 496, each across 21 suites. macOS full just release-check passed 501 ordinary plus 501 instrumented tests; required coverage is 100 percent: 13141 lines, 1362 functions, 21955 regions, 3152 branches. Linux and Windows full aggregate jobs are still running. The earlier incomplete-install Bun attempt is excluded."
  "2026-10-19T16:58:51.043Z",codex-agent,"All nine CI jobs at ceffe36 are green in run 39285340550. Full just release-check passed on all three OSes: Linux 505 ordinary plus 505 instrumented tests, macOS 501 plus 501, Windows 496 plus 496; each has 42 suite executions, zero failures/ignored tests, and 100 percent lines/functions/regions/branches at unchanged scope/thresholds. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, required locked-oracle tests, audit, changelog, clone-local merge drivers and strict check-only project health passed. CodeQL checks passed. With stronger complete three-OS certification available, stopped the redundant isolated local aggregate before completion; it is excluded from passing evidence. Final evidence/hand-off commit will receive a fresh matrix and final-head clone health before STOP."
  "2026-10-19T16:59:58.104Z",codex-agent,"Review round 1 handoff: all three CodeRabbit findings fixed with behavioral revert proofs; both original CI failures diagnosed and repaired without raising latency ceilings, lowering coverage or changing the oracle pin. Evidence: docs/benchmarks/native-context-review-1-2026-10-19.json and docs/NATIVE_CONTEXT_SECTIONS.md. Preserve pinned upstream behavior tracked by pm-cli issues 1509 through 1513. All nine source-head CI jobs and CodeQL passed; Bun 25/25, linked tests 5/5 commands (13 underlying executions), Node harness 4/4, synthetic end-to-end parity 37/37. Releasing this item open for orchestrator verification. Final evidence-only push will receive fresh full three-OS CI and exact-head clean-clone check-only health before reporting STOP. No thread replies/resolutions, merges or releases performed. Existing local extension-version skew remains outside this slice; no new CLI/SDK bug was found."
  "2026-10-19T19:26:43.203Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2: fetched remote PR 98 head 090d799; origin/main is an ancestor, so no merge or reconcile is required. Read all comments on all four unresolved threads and the latest CodeRabbit review body (no outside-diff findings). The older argument and external-root findings are already fixed with regressions; reverify their behavior-only revert proofs. Correct the two valid documentation findings, add documentation contract regressions with independent reversion checks, run unchanged just release-check and Bun oracle acceptance, and verify fresh-clone health plus exact pushed-head CI. Preserve the pinned TS contracts tracked by pm-cli issues 1509 through 1513. No review replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-19T19:27:20.095Z",codex-agent,"Verified four independent revert proofs using node --test --test-name-pattern=<selection> scripts/harness.test.mts: remove only argument option-token rejection => required options fails, exit 1; remove only source_kind exclusion => packet roots fails on colliding plain global/external IDs, exit 1; restore only README to 090d799 => README advertises fails, exit 1; restore only orientation documentation to 090d799 => orientation documentation fails, exit 1. Each identical selected command passes after byte-exact restoration (exit 0); restored complete harness passes 6/6. Documentation changes accurately describe configured defaults, brief ten-group omission, full all-section selection and settings-disabled deep sections; full depth also avoids the ordinary default ten-row cap. Runtime TS parity and thresholds remain unchanged. Older threads PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uAIel and PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uAIew need no further implementation: required arguments already reject option tokens; root selection already excludes global/external namespaces, and the existing real-tracker external differential covers eight full/summary TOON/JSON cases."
  "2026-10-19T19:28:20.184Z",codex-agent,"All five linked pm test commands passed with zero skipped selections; Node harness is now 6/6, and all 15 underlying test executions passed. Project policy keeps run recording disabled (tracking_disabled), so results are recorded here. Changelog regeneration and verification passed. Local check-only strict health has the inherited global pm-github host skew (locked host 2026.10.14 versus installed extension 2026.10.19); verify project-only health in an isolated fresh clone without changing either pin or global extensions. The files command accepts one --add value per invocation; a rejected multi-value call was retried as separate explicit writes."
  "2026-10-19T19:29:24.926Z",codex-agent,"Evidence timing correction: the prior linked-test checkpoint was read from an existing scratch log before the current invocation initialized its output. It must not be treated as this round completed-run evidence. The fresh pm test run is active; final counts and exits will be recorded only after completion. The four independent reversion checks and restored 6/6 Node run were fresh and are confirmed."
  "2026-10-19T19:39:33.390Z",codex-agent,"Fresh current-run acceptance confirmed: pm test pm-rust-s6j4 --run --progress exited 0 with all five commands passed and no skipped selections (15 underlying executions: 1 deep-section unit, 6 packet units, 1 completion differential, 6 Node harness tests, 1 namespace differential containing eight output comparisons). Run receipt remains tracking_disabled by existing policy. Fresh git clone --no-local of 10aee76 with isolated home and global Git configuration passed merge installation and health --check-only --require-merge-drivers --strict-exit, exit 0, with no tracked changes. Existing advisories remain; this is not a full retained-history audit. Three-OS CI latency passed unchanged 50/150/250ms get/list/context bounds; context p95 Linux 108.286ms, macOS 140.395ms, Windows 193.425ms. Full aggregate gates and Bun acceptance remain pending."
  "2026-10-19T20:03:00.344Z",codex-agent,"Review round 2 certification at 10aee76 PASSED in CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-rust/actions/runs/39311368978: unchanged just release-check on Linux 505 ordinary + 505 instrumented, macOS 501 + 501, Windows 496 + 496; each 42 suite executions, zero failures or ignored tests. Required coverage is 100 percent lines/functions/regions/branches on every OS. Exact covered totals in that order: Linux 13094/1350/21868/3150; macOS 13141/1362/21955/3152; Windows 13140/1363/21956/3154. Formatting, strict Clippy, private-item rustdoc, pinned-oracle suites, audit under the existing policy, changelog and clone-local tracker health passed. All nine CI jobs plus CodeQL are green. Bun 1.3.5 acceptance command PM_NODE_INTERPRETER=bun PM_RUST_REQUIRE_PUBLISHED_CLI=1 cargo test --locked --test orientation_differential passed 25/25, zero failed or ignored. This Rust repository has no root npm manifest; just release-check plus Bun differential acceptance is its documented equivalent. All five pm-linked commands passed, totaling 15 underlying executions; tracking_disabled policy is unchanged."
  "2026-10-19T20:03:06.693Z",codex-agent,"Review handoff: all four unresolved threads are addressed. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uAIel already rejects option-token argument values; PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uAIew already filters plain global/external root namespaces and tests external packet behavior. PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uD-aw now documents configured depth and settings-dependent omissions; PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uD-a0 now lists full depth in README. Independent revert commands: node --test --test-name-pattern=\"required options\" scripts/harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"packet roots\" scripts/harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"orientation documentation\" scripts/harness.test.mts; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"README advertises\" scripts/harness.test.mts. Each exits 1 when only its corresponding guard/document correction is reverted and exits 0 after byte-exact restoration. Complete harness passes 6/6. No invalid finding required refusal; no outside-diff findings were present. Preserve TS quirks tracked by pm-cli issues 1509 through 1513. Existing host-only pm-github skew is outside scope; isolated fresh-clone strict check-only health passes with existing advisories. No new pm CLI/SDK bug found. Release ownership without closing; final tracker-only push will receive fresh exact-head CI and clone health verification, recorded on PR 98. No thread replies/resolutions, merges or releases."
  "2026-10-19T21:45:37.655Z",codex-agent,"PR #98 review round: four unresolved threads fetched with all comments; latest review has no outside-diff findings. Branch includes origin/main. Validate nested authoritative snapshots, matching packet refusals, adjacency traversal, and rendered-budget error semantics against the pinned oracle; add behavioral revert proofs and run the unchanged just release-check gate."
  "2026-10-19T21:48:34.374Z",codex-agent,"Verified PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uG8gW against pinned SDK dependencies.js: isContextBudgetFloorError uses startsWith(\"Relationship context tokenBudget cannot fit \"), so both root/evidence and one-node floors retain smallestResult after a successful attempt. Changing only native behavior would break pm-cli#1513 parity. Keep behavior, clarify docs, and add a root-only rendered-budget differential. Other three findings are valid and being fixed with regressions."
  "2026-10-19T21:54:29.296Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: root-only cache exclusions now preserve nested authoritative item/history snapshots; packet parity compares status and complete bytes and stops continuation after a matching refusal; graph incident edges are indexed once, and traversal/direct-role counts/fingerprint are reused across rendered-budget retries. Node and Bun harness tests pass 7/7. Snapshot-only behavioral reversion fails 0/1 (exit 1), restored 1/1; reverting only the packet comparison fails the real-tracker harness at packet comparison 9 (exit 101). Remaining adjacency and oracle-divergence proofs are running before the aggregate gates."
  "2026-10-19T21:56:48.743Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral proof: reverting only Graph::neighbors to the previous full-edge scan compiles and fails packet_adjacency_bounds_unrelated_edge_work (exit 101; 134.87 seconds for the reverted test); restoring the index passes all 8 packet tests (exit 0). Applying the requested one-node-only fallback to read fails relationship_root_evidence_floor_retains_oracle_parity: native exit 1 versus oracle exit 0 for a root-only 100-token packet. Restoring oracle-compatible fallback passes (exit 0). Refusal is therefore retained for PRRT_kwDOTwgMRs6uG8gW with pm-cli#1513 evidence. Adjacency also bounds emitted-edge candidate selection; stable global edge order is preserved."
  "2026-10-19T22:00:30.562Z",codex-agent,"Final-source linked validation passed all 7 commands and 20 underlying test executions, with zero failures/skips/empty runs. The final 6000-character evidence fixture accepts matching initial and continuation packet refusals and writes its immutable-copy receipt; reverting only the matrix status comparison fails at comparison 1 (exit 101), restored execution passes. Project policy disables automatic test-run recording, so this comment retains the aggregate. Starting unchanged just release-check with isolated HOME/Git configuration, followed by the complete Bun orientation differential suite."
  "2026-10-19T22:02:21.380Z",codex-agent,"The isolated aggregate stopped at strict Clippy before tests: emitted-edge candidate indexing used flat_map on Option. Replaced it with filter_map plus the existing flatten, preserving the selected edge positions and order; no lint or coverage thresholds changed. Restarting the complete aggregate after the correction."
  "2026-10-19T22:31:17.353Z",codex-agent,"Review implementation is complete. All 7 linked commands (20 underlying executions), Node/Bun harness tests (7 each), strict Clippy, fmt, and changelog checks pass. Three valid threads have behavioral revert proofs; the fourth proposed change demonstrably breaks pinned-oracle parity. The isolated full aggregate and complete Bun orientation suite are still running without failures. Commit and push this implementation to start exact-head three-platform CI concurrently; retain the claim until certification and final tracker handoff. Existing history records remain byte-identical; all tracker changes are appended."
